{"type":"text","timestamp":1788217879633,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eba7fdffec2uHvZPcMB5MvE","part":{"id":"prt_05a173b89001tK0Jfqa2zoMs4y","messageID":"msg_05a171375001Z57ron1rcOOG93","sessionID":"ses_fa5eba7fdffec2uHvZPcMB5MvE","type":"text","text":"Now I understand the architecture. Let me create the `--explain-offload` diagnostic module.\n\n","time":{"start":1788217867145,"end":1788217879625}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788217879644,"sessionID":"ses_fa5eba7fdffec2uHvZPcMB5MvE","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1b1f5749ca692a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-168/src/offload.rs","content":"//! The `--explain-offload` diagnostic: which sub-expressions are offloadable and which\n//! fall back to scalar evaluation, and why.\n//!\n//! Vectorizability is silent and cardinality-derived (plans/questions.md Q8): a\n//! sub-expression is admissible for offload exactly when its cardinality is known --\n//! `One`, `Opt`, or a `fold` over a collection -- and not admissible when it is a\n//! `Stream`, whose extent is unbounded. The design's offload boundary and its layer\n//! boundary are the same boundary (draft.md, \"Cardinality is the kernel-admissibility\n//! predicate\"): everything in the value layer is a kernel candidate, and the effect\n//! layer is exactly what cannot be one.\n//!\n//! This is diagnostic-only. It computes nothing the backends do not already decide from\n//! the same types, and it changes neither the type system nor any signature. The flag\n//! just makes the otherwise-silent decision visible.\n\nuse crate::tir::{Kind, Program, Tir};\nuse crate::ty::Type;\n\n/// The cardinality of an expression, read off its type. Admissibility is a property of\n/// the type, not of the operation (draft.md, \"The admissible input set\").\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\nenum Cardinality {\n    /// Exactly one value per input: a scalar.\n    One,\n    /// Zero or one: an Opt, admissible as stream compaction.\n    Opt,\n    /// A collection of known extent: a fold over a Vec.\n    Fold,\n    /// Unbounded extent: a Stream. The only inadmissible cardinality.\n    Stream,\n}\n\nimpl Cardinality {\n    fn label(self) -> &'static str {\n        match self {\n            Cardinality::One => \"One\",\n            Cardinality::Opt => \"Opt\",\n            Cardinality::Fold => \"fold\",\n            Cardinality::Stream => \"Stream\",\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Whether a sub-expression of this cardinality is admissible for offload. Only a\n    /// Stream is not: its extent is unknown, so it cannot be a kernel and must fall back\n    /// to scalar evaluation.\n    fn admissible(self) -> bool {\n        self != Cardinality::Stream\n    }\n}\n\n/// The cardinality an expression carries, from its type. A `Stream` is outermost and\n/// always wins when present; otherwise a `Vec` is a fold over known-extent data, an\n/// `Opt` is stream compaction, and anything else is a scalar `One`.\nfn cardinality(ty: &Type) -> Cardinality {\n    if matches!(ty, Type::Stream(_)) {\n        Cardinality::Stream\n    } else if ty.contains_vec() {\n        Cardinality::Fold\n    } else if ty.as_opt().is_some() {\n        Cardinality::Opt\n    } else {\n        Cardinality::One\n    }\n}\n\n/// The report: one line per sub-expression, in pre-order, across every function and the\n/// program body. Each line names the sub-expression, its cardinality, and whether that\n/// cardinality makes it an offloadable kernel or a scalar fallback.\npub fn explain(program: &Program) -> String {\n    let mut out = String::new();\n    out.push_str(\"explain offload: vectorizability by cardinality\\n\");\n    for f in &program.funcs {\n        out.push_str(&format!(\"function {}:\\n\", f.name));\n        walk(&f.body, 1, &mut out);\n    }\n    out.push_str(\"program body:\\n\");\n    walk(&program.body, 1, &mut out);\n    out\n}\n\nfn walk(t: &Tir, depth: usize, out: &mut String) {\n    let card = cardinality(&t.ty);\n    let disposition = if card.admissible() {\n        \"offloadable kernel\"\n    } else {\n        \"scalar fallback\"\n    };\n    out.push_str(&format!(\n        \"{}{} : {} -- {} -- {}\\n\",\n        \"  \".repeat(depth),\n        kind_name(&t.kind),\n        t.ty,\n        card.label(),\n        disposition\n    ));\n    match &t.kind {\n        Kind::Str(_)\n        | Kind::Int(_)\n        | Kind::Var(_)\n        | Kind::Local(_)\n        | Kind::Input\n        | Kind::Inputs\n        | Kind::Lines => {}\n        Kind::VecLit(items) => items.iter().for_each(|i| walk(i, depth + 1, out)),\n        Kind::RecordLit { fields } => {\n            fields.iter().for_each(|(_, v)| walk(v, depth + 1, out))\n        }\n        Kind::EnumLit { payload, .. } => {\n            if let Some(p) = payload {\n                walk(p, depth + 1, out);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Call { arg, .. } => {\n            if let Some(a) = arg {\n                walk(a, depth + 1, out);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Concat(l, r)\n        | Kind::Compare { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. }\n        | Kind::Logic { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. }\n        | Kind::Arith { lhs: l, rhs: r, .. } => {\n            walk(l, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(r, depth + 1, out);\n        }\n        Kind::Not(base) => walk(base, depth + 1, out),\n        Kind::Cond {\n            cond,\n            then,\n            otherwise,\n        } => {\n            walk(cond, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(then, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(otherwise, depth + 1, out);\n        }\n        Kind::Bind { value, body, .. } => {\n            walk(value, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(body, depth + 1, out);\n        }\n        Kind::Map { source, body, .. } | Kind::OptMap { source, body, .. } => {\n            walk(source, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(body, depth + 1, out);\n        }\n        Kind::Select { source, pred, .. } => {\n            walk(source, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(pred, depth + 1, out);\n        }\n        Kind::Field { base, .. } | Kind::Unwrap { base } => walk(base, depth + 1, out),\n        Kind::Builtin { arg, .. } => walk(arg, depth + 1, out),\n        Kind::Index { base, index, .. } => {\n            walk(base, depth + 1, out);\n            walk(index, depth + 1, out);\n        }\n        Kind::Slice { base, start, end, .. } => {\n            walk(base, depth + 1, out);\n            if let Some(s) = start {\n                walk(s, depth + 1, out);\n            }\n            if let Some(e) = end {\n                walk(e, depth + 1, out);\n            }\n        }\n        Kind::Match { subject, arms, .. } => {\n            walk(subject, depth + 1, out);\n            for arm in arms {\n                if let Some(g) = &arm.guard {\n                    walk(g, depth + 1, out);\n                }\n                walk(&arm.body, depth + 1, out);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfn kind_name(k: &Kind) -> &'static str {\n    match k {\n        Kind::Str(_) => \"str\",\n        Kind::Int(_) => \"int\",\n        Kind::VecLit(_) => \"vec-literal\",\n        Kind::RecordLit { .. } => \"record-literal\",\n        Kind::EnumLit { .. } => \"enum-literal\",\n        Kind::OptMap { .. } => \"opt-map\",\n        Kind::Var(_) => \"var\",\n        Kind::Local(_) => \"local\",\n        Kind::Input => \"input\",\n        Kind::Inputs => \"inputs\",\n        Kind::Lines => \"lines\",\n        Kind::Call { .. } => \"call\",\n        Kind::Concat(..) => \"concat\",\n        Kind::Arith { .. } => \"arith\",\n        Kind::Cond { .. } => \"cond\",\n        Kind::Compare { .. } => \"compare\",\n        Kind::Logic { .. } => \"logic\",\n        Kind::Not(_) => \"not\",\n        Kind::Bind { .. } => \"bind\",\n        Kind::Map { .. } => \"map\",\n        Kind::Select { .. } => \"select\",\n        Kind::Field { .. } => \"field\",\n        Kind::Builtin { .. } => \"builtin\",\n        Kind::Unwrap { .. } => \"unwrap\",\n        Kind::Index { .. } => \"index\",\n        Kind::Slice { .. } => \"slice\",\n        Kind::Match { .. } => \"match\",\n    }\n}\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-168/src/offload.rs","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"src/offload.rs","time":{"start":1788217879619,"end":1788217879640}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good. Now let me verify the `Type` implements Display (it does, `write!(f, ...)` earlier). And `Type::Sink` — is `contains_vec` defined at line 237. Let me check the exact signature.\n\nNow let me write the offload module. Let me decide on kind_name helper for readable node labels. Actually, rather than mapping every Kind to a name, I could use the debug representation? Kind doesn't derive Debug. Let me just produce a small label via a match, or better: describe the node by its type and a generic marker. \n\nActually, to keep it simpler and stable for snapshots, let me not label by Kind exhaustively. Instead, for each node I'll print its cardinality and disposition plus its type, and a human label for the top-level kinds that matter. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider the report granularity. Reporting EVERY node (including Int literals) is noisy. But the issue explicitly wants \"which sub-expressions became vectorized/offloaded kernels and which fell back to scalar evaluation\". That's about every sub-expression. I'll report every node. For identification, I'll give each node a short kind name.\n\nLet me write kind_name for all kinds. That's a chunk but fine.\n\nActually, maybe a cleaner and less noisy report: report the *cardinality boundary* — each node grouped by disposition. But that loses which node. Let me just do per-node lines with kind name. I'll write a `kind_name` match.\n\nLet me write the module now.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to report every node or to be more surgical. The issue: \"which sub-expressions became vectorized/offloaded kernels and which fell back to scalar evaluation, and why\". A straightforward per-sub-expression report is the most faithful. Let me do it.\n\nLet me define the output format to be stable:\n\n```\nexplain offload\n  <kind> : <ty> -> <Cardinality> (admissible: offloadable kernel | inadmissible: scalar fallback)\n```\n\nLet me write it. I'll include the cardinality label and a disposition word. Format per line:\n\n`<indent><kind> : <ty> -- <label> -- <offloadable kernel|scalar fallback>`\n\nLet me write kind_name. I'll produce lowercase short names.\n\nNow write src/offload.rs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05a173d59001dDyB5CBY74LfTG","sessionID":"ses_fa5eba7fdffec2uHvZPcMB5MvE","messageID":"msg_05a171375001Z57ron1rcOOG93"}}
